# Skill: sprint-report

Generate the end-of-sprint QA AI-usage report from the activity tracker.

## When to invoke

At the end of each sprint (or on demand), to produce the report sent to the team/manager.

## Step 1 — Verify the tracker is up to date

```bash
python scripts/qa_track.py status
```

Look for any record that is still missing `--manual` or `--automated` counts. Fill them
in before generating the report — never generate from incomplete data.

## Step 2 — Generate the report

```bash
python scripts/qa_track.py report --sprint <sprint-id>
```

The report outputs a table with one row per ticket:

| Ticket | Title | Manual TCs | Automated TCs | Basis | Reason (if automated < manual) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| TICKET-1 | ... | N | M | ac/plan/both | ... |

## Step 3 — Review for accuracy

Before sending:

- Count only what actually exists. If tests were planned but not written, they are not
  automated test cases.
- Never invent a number to fill a cell. Leave it at 0 and say so.
- The tracked time is **assisted wall-clock time** — not the total time on the ticket,
  not human hours per activity. Never present it as either.

## Step 4 — Distribute

Share the report with the team via {{ tracker_label }} or {{ doc_label }}, per your
team's sprint review process.
